 Runtime role for outbound and inbound mail: notification delivery,
 invitation and onboarding messages, DKIM signing, and milter-based spam
 filtering.

Package: drumee-role-schemas
Architecture: all
Section: database
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-schemas (= ${drumee:SchemasVersion}),
         drumee-patch (= ${drumee:PatchVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23),
         mariadb-client,
         mariadb-backup
Description: Drumee schema role (database init and migration jobs)
 Runtime role for the run-once containers that create the yp/utils/template
 databases, seed the entity pool and system accounts, and apply pending
 schema patches before the application role is allowed to start.
 .
 The packages install migration payloads under /usr/share/drumee/patches
 only. Nothing touches the database at package configuration time, because
 no database exists during an image build. Application is driven by this
 role's entrypoint at deploy time and recorded in the schema_migrations
 table, which makes it idempotent and lets the application role refuse to
 start against an under-migrated database.

Package: drumee-role-infra
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Provides: drumee-role
Conflicts: drumee-role
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         drumee-release (= ${binary:Version}),
         drumee-infra (= ${drumee:InfraVersion}),
         drumee-bootstrap (= ${drumee:BootstrapVersion}),
         drumee-node-runtime (= ${drumee:NodeRuntimeVersion}),
         nodejs (>= 22),
         nodejs (<< 23)
Description: Drumee infrastructure role (configuration rendering job)
 Runtime role for the run-once container that renders the service
 configuration tree from the deployment's environment, writing it to the
 shared configuration volume consumed by the other roles.
 .
 Rendering happens in a chroot-style target directory, so this role never
 writes to a host path and never reconfigures the machine it runs on.
